// Self-assessment tests for the textbook "Intelligent Systems"
$CATEGORY: Intelligent Systems

// Chapter 1, question 1
::C1.1:: What distinguishes knowledge from information in the "data – information – knowledge" hierarchy? {
~knowledge is always numeric, while information is text
~knowledge takes up more memory than information
~knowledge needs no context and is equally clear to everyone
=knowledge contains regularities that make it possible to draw conclusions and act
}

// Chapter 1, question 2
::C1.2:: Which property is NOT a characteristic feature of an intelligent system? {
~work with incomplete and inaccurate input information
~the ability to explain the conclusions obtained to the user
=executing only a rigidly programmed algorithm
~the ability to learn from new data and experience
}

// Chapter 1, question 3
::C1.3:: What is an expert system? {
~a database that stores the contacts and qualifications of the organization's experts for quick search
=a system that uses specialists' knowledge to solve problems in a narrow domain
~any program with a graphical interface for specialists in a field
~a neural network trained on big data without human involvement
}

